# Sealed exemplar figures are content-addressed by dsx seal (spec.visuals[].svg_sha256).
# They must be stored byte-exact so the seal survives commit/checkout on any platform —
# never line-ending-normalised. matplotlib writes the repo's native CRLF on Windows; the
# recorded seals are of those exact bytes and the off-gate-path double-render determinism
# test re-renders on the same platform. Marking them binary preserves both.
examples/figures/*.svg binary

# Profiler reference fixtures are content-addressed by `dsx profile` (`source_hash` is
# a sha256 of the file's exact bytes, and the committed golden records that hash). They
# must survive commit/checkout on any platform byte-exact, exactly like the sealed
# figures above -- never line-ending-normalised. Found 2026-09-10 at the v2.6 ship
# check: on a CRLF checkout the hash no longer matched the golden recorded from an LF
# working copy.
tests/fixtures/profiler/*.csv -text
